[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    106[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Not differentially testable (undefined behaviour in the C)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    107[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    108[0m:[38;5;10m[49m These are real rejection-adjacent inputs, but the C's answer is *indeterminate*,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    109[0m:[38;5;10m[49m so "byte-identical" is not a meaningful assertion. They are excluded from the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    110[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Phase C suite by construction, and the reason is recorded here rather than being
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    111[0m:[38;5;10m[49m silently skipped:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    112[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    113[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - Row #46 / `c2GJK` with `typeA` or `typeB` out of range: `c2MakeProxy` writes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    114[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   nothing, so C proceeds with an **uninitialised** `c2Proxy` on the stack
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    115[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`pA.count`, `pA.verts[0]`, `pA.radius` are garbage). Rust zero-initialises.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    116[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   No implementation can match indeterminate stack contents.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    117[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `c2GJK` with `cache->count > 3`: C reads `cache->iA[3]` (past the array, into
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    118[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the `iB`/`div` fields) and then writes `saveA[3]` past a 3-element stack array.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    119[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   Rust panics on the bounds check instead. UB in C.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    120[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `c2GJK` with a cache whose `iA[i]`/`iB[i]` index at or beyond the proxy's
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    121[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `count`: in C, `pA.verts[iA]` for `iA` in `[count, 8)` reads uninitialised
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    122[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (but in-bounds) struct bytes; for `iA >= 8` or `iA < 0` it reads off the end
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    123[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   of the struct entirely. Rust reads zeros / panics. UB in C.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    124[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - Null `c2Simplex*` / `c2Proxy*` / `c2v*` out-pointers to `c22`, `c23`, `c2D`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    125[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `c2L`, `c2Witness`, `c2Support`, `c2MakeProxy`, `c2BBVerts`: the C has no null
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    126[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   check on these and segfaults. Both sides crash; nothing to compare.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    127[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (Only `c2GJK` checks its pointers — rows #27-#32 — and those *are* tested.)
